{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>As he interpreted</b> — in gematria: dreams follow the mouth:" "<b>(</b> כהנה. Twice in the Masorah: here and the other: ואם מעט ואוסיפה לך כהנה. Thus Scripture says: ומוצא אני מר ממות את האשה, and this is ואוסיפה לך כהנה — for had she been evil, I would not have seen כהנה for evil."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {1 "The comment glosses the second occurrence (Exodus 1:10) by quoting Ecclesiastes 7:26 and arguing that Pharaoh's addendum 'כהנה' could not apply had the woman (Israel) been evil; the cryptic juxtaposition is preserved as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:09.211331005Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}